From 2c9d79af073964cbed2f738518db181c0904f0a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:59:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Heidenhain G205 writes the retraction feed Q208 as
 a number

An iTNC 530 programming station (NC software 606425 004 SP20) refuses
the whole G205 block on a DIN/ISO import when it reads Q208=FMAX. The
post now writes Q208=+99999.999, the top of the documented input range
(iTNC 530 cycle manual 670388-25, cycle 205; its own example writes
Q208=99999). The TNC 640 takes the same number.

The Heidenhain cycle tests now fail on any Q value that is not a signed
number. The drill_peck golden changes in that one word.

Fixes #3102

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
